    "title": "Leonardo DiCaprio and Jeff Bezos backed a $200 million pledge for 100 threatened species, from pangolins and salamanders to rare wild pigs | Hindustan Times",
    "text": "Where the money comes from and where it goes\nThe money came from a few different sources. Of the $200 million promised at launch, $100 million came from the Bezos Earth Fund. Another $100 million came from Re:wild, supported by DiCaprio, Age of Union and the Todd Graves Family Foundation. The 100 species are mammals, birds, fish, plants and more, from 30 countries. The work will be led by more than 100 partners, including Indigenous Peoples, local communities and governments, Re:wild said. The IUCN Species Survival Commission was a knowledge partner. Its goal is to help ensure the science remains rigorous. Barney Long of Re:wild said each species would get five years of support so teams wouldn't be chasing short grants.",
